## 1.4.0

All four board corners now have the 1 mm radius. USB-C J2 moved 1.5 mm down
from the top edge (centre y 105.4 -> 106.9) so its shell clears the rounded
top-left corner; the mouth still overhangs the left edge by 1.2 mm.
USB-side stubs re-routed; the VBUS A9 +5V feed now runs on B.Cu to the
existing via beside U1 so it does not cross CC2. JLCPCB export regenerated.

## 1.3.0

USB-C J2 moved to the top-left corner, which is now square (other corners
keep the 1 mm radius). The receptacle mouth overhangs the left edge by
1.2 mm (as in modules/usb-power) so any plug overmold clears the board.
USB-side routing redone; R3 rotated so CC1 meets it from the top.
build_pcb.py now finishes with a native kicad-cli zone refill + save: the
in-script fill ignored the project edge/hole clearances, so the 1.1.0/1.2.0
saved boards and Gerbers had GND pour up to the board edge and the J2 NPTH
holes (the shared check refills before DRC, which hid it). JLCPCB export
regenerated.

## 1.2.0

C4 +5V bulk 100uF 6.3V (C15008) -> 22uF 25V X5R 1206 (C12891, Basic),
so it meets the 80 % voltage-derating rule at USB's 5.25 V maximum.
Same footprint and placement; JLCPCB export regenerated.

## 1.1.0

J1 is now a 1x05 2.54 mm header: 1 UPDI (out to the module), 2-4 GND,
5 SELF (this board's own UPDI). Silkscreen UPDI/GND/GND/GND/SELF.
UPDI output net renamed PROG -> UPDI; activity LED silk PROG -> ACT.
LCSC/MPN/manufacturer fields on every assembled part (red power LED,
white activity LED); J1 is hand-soldered and excluded from the CPL.
First JLCPCB export in jlcpcb/.

## 1.0.0

Big Modular version of the Bread Modular UPDIProgrammer 0.3.0.
Same USB-C / CH340N / ATtiny1616 (jtag2updi) circuit and firmware.
Replace the Bread Modular GND1/NC1/OUTPUT1 headers and the 330R ground
resistor with one 1x04 2.54 mm header: PROG, GND, GND, SELF (own UPDI).
Drop the serial TX/RX header pins.
New 42 x 18 mm 2-layer layout with GND pours, generated by tools/.
